{# One noul question, as a Jinja2 template.

   The server renders this once per Gmail label and sends all of them in a
   single Jev request, keyed by label ID.

   `{{ label.name }}` has to appear in `instructions`. Question IDs are never
   shown to the model, so the rendered instructions are everything it knows
   about a label. Leave the name out and every question renders identically,
   which makes every answer meaningless. The server checks for this at startup
   and refuses to run without it.

   The instructions are built as one string and then passed through `tojson`,
   rather than written as a quoted JSON string with values dropped into it. A
   label named `"Urgent"` carries quote marks, and `tojson` is what keeps those
   from ending the string early.

   Available variables.

     label.name
     label.description   empty when nothing is stored for the label
     thread.*            the same variables STATE.json lists

   A noul answer is a probability from 0 to 1 rather than a yes or a no. The
   server compares it to the threshold.
#}
{% set meaning = " That label means " ~ label.description ~ "." if label.description else "" %}
{
  "type": "noul",
  "instructions": {{ ('The Gmail label "' ~ label.name ~ '" belongs on this email thread.' ~ meaning) | tojson }},
  "criteria": {
    "true": "The thread's content clearly falls under this label.",
    "false": "The thread is unrelated to this label, or only mentions it in passing."
  }
}
